[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615719503","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2615719503","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2615719503,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b6LZP","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T13:08:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T13:12:55Z","body":"Yup a templated function was my first thought too, however I was suspecting the reason for using a define was to try and remove the work of the string concatenation:\r\n\r\nFor instance\r\n```\r\nprint_verbose(\"blah blah\" + \"blah\" + itos(a));\r\n```\r\nWith a templated function, will it do the concatenation work, even though it will not be used further on? Or does the variable  args remove this problem?\r\n\r\nWith the define, if the `is_print_verbose_enabled()` fails, it should avoid the string concatenation.\r\n\r\nThere is a note about this in the source:\r\n```\r\n// This version avoids processing the text to be printed until it actually has to be printed, saving some CPU usage.\r\n#define print_verbose(m_text)             \\\r\n\t{                                     \\\r\n\t\tif (is_print_verbose_enabled()) { \\\r\n\t\t\tprint_line(m_text);           \\\r\n\t\t}                                 \\\r\n\t}\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615719503/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615748808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2615748808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2615748808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b6SjI","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T13:21:06Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T13:22:58Z","body":"Right. That makes sense, I suppose.\r\nThen I would say the best solution would be a full project find and replace of `print_verbose` -> `PRINT_VERBOSE`. The reason macros are usually uppercase is precisely to avoid this kind of issue, where it interferes with normal function usage.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615748808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615771100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2615771100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2615771100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6b6X_c","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-27T13:31:04Z","updated_at":"2025-01-27T13:31:04Z","body":"I do agree on capitalization for macros, mind you that approach might be subject to more push back (as the change is less localized), and will require rebasing existing PRs that use `print_verbose`.\r\n\r\nI wouldn't be surprised if this was historically a function and later changed to a macro for the string concat efficiency.\r\n\r\nProbably better for a separate PR though, so preferred approach can be chosen in a meeting.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2615771100/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2623811544","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2623811544","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2623811544,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cZC_Y","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T08:16:00Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T08:16:00Z","body":"> Then I would say the best solution would be a full project find and replace of `print_verbose` -> `PRINT_VERBOSE`. The reason macros are usually uppercase is precisely to avoid this kind of issue, where it interferes with normal function usage.\r\n\r\nThere is already a PR to do exactly that: #100224.\r\n\r\nBut indeed, as I commented there, `print_verbose` is meant to look and feel like a function because it's similar to the `print_line` and `print_error` functions.\r\n\r\nBut its argument can often be costly to compute, hence why it was made a macro to avoid paying that cost. That makes it possible to use `print_verbose` relatively liberally without worrying too much that this will have a performance impact in production builds.\r\n\r\nWhether that's a premature optimization, this would likely be worth testing.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2623811544/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624106856","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2624106856","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2624106856,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6caLFo","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T10:32:46Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T10:32:46Z","body":"Realized it would be better to call this new macro from FUNCBINDVARARGV, to reduce the code duplication and make it clearer, have re-pushed, should be clearer now what is going on.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624106856/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624121556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2624121556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2624121556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6caOrU","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T10:39:12Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T10:39:12Z","body":"> Whether that's a premature optimization, this would likely be worth testing.\r\n\r\nThe macro approach is definitely worth doing - I was doing some profiling a couple of days ago with a similar logging macro, and the cost of concatenating strings that will never be printed is indeed significant.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624121556/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624190251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2624190251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2624190251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cafcr","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T11:08:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T11:08:59Z","body":"When I brought up premature optimization i failed to consider that the argument evaluation could be deferred; i thought it may only try to avoid a call. It being a macro makes more sense to me now!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624190251/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2625166818","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102062#issuecomment-2625166818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102062","id":2625166818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ceN3i","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T17:42:52Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T17:42:52Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2625166818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]